  factText: Mycelium is the hidden rootlike network of fungi, a web of tiny threads
    (hyphae) spreading through soil. It grows into dead wood and leaves, breaking
    them down. This decomposition releases nutrients back into the earth, feeding
    new plant and mushroom growth.
